WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.437
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:03.425
The engine is only half the chain.

3
00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:05.589
The other half is a connection string,

4
00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:08.800
and most of them hold a password
or a Windows credential.

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.968
Until each string moves to an Entra mode,

6
00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:14.712
the application keeps the instance
tied to Windows Authentication.

7
00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:19.496
In this module you list every sequel server
connection string an application holds,

8
00:00:19.496 --> 00:00:21.888
and say which ones
carry a stored password.

9
00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:25.491
Then you say whether each move
is a configuration change,

10
00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:29.325
a driver or code change, the
vendor's decision, or already done.

11
00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:31.990
No string changes until
the three gates hold.
